{ignore}
<p><code>{progress}</code> shows how far something has got. It writes the native
<code>&lt;progress value max&gt;</code> element, styled on the server
(<code>lib/progress.php</code>), under a line with the label and the rounded percentage -
no script, and it prints. The value is clamped to 0 ... <code>max</code>.</p>

<p>With <code>steps</code> it draws a row of dots instead, one per step up to
<code>max</code>, joined by a line: the steps up to the value filled and the current one
ringed - a checkout or a wizard. The steps are <code>role="progressbar"</code> with
<code>aria-valuenow</code>, <code>-min</code>, <code>-max</code> and
<code>aria-valuetext="Step 3 of 5"</code>.</p>

<p>The visible label line is <code>aria-hidden</code>, since the bar carries the same text as
its <code>aria-label</code> - it is not read twice. <code>color</code> picks a slot and
<code>size</code> the thickness. The colours are <code>--pad-progress-track</code>,
<code>-text</code> and one per slot on <code>.pad-progress</code>, with
<code>light-dark()</code> defaults written once per page.</p>

<p>A value that is no number, a max that is not above 0 (or for steps not a whole number up
to 50), an unknown color or size is an error under the strict check.</p>
{/ignore}
